  "interpretation": [
    "A common physical reflection-antisymmetric shape grows across all seven saved fields and four controllers, with a rate matching the observed2840s offset amplification. This describes the actual saved trajectory; it does not establish a unique full Jacobian at nearly zero membrane velocity.",
    "For positive phase displacement, leading-edge bound and unbound MCA decrease, Rac increases and Rho decreases; both lower boundMCA and lowerRho increase localRac production. Tension increases there, which supplies an opposing tension-to-Rho activation route.",
    "The common cutRac trace has no antisymmetric first-order variation. The common signed protrusion-command variation is supplied by opposite flank-tension perturbations; it nearly offsets the native absolute-controller relaxation.",
    "Odd scalar pool perturbations integrate tozero. The odd central change of globaluniformreturn is therefore zero to numericalprecision in the selected reflection-paired steps. Even responses are recorded separately because the native unbound upwind map may be nonsmooth atW\u22480.",
    "At12000s a small symmetric relaxation transient is still larger than the extremely tinyodd component. At24000\u201330060s the change of the symmetric part fromthe originalbasal is only about1e\u22125\u20135e\u22125 ofthe odd-fieldRMS, so the late saved growth is strongly odd dominated."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "No continuum instability or asymptotic eigenmode claim follows from these discretized finite-time profiles.",
    "A one-step source allocation is not an evolved pathwayablation or a unique cause of thegrowthrate.",
    "Native donor switching at almostzero membranevelocity makes the full map potentially nondifferentiable. A reproducible odd observed shape and odd central projection do not prove differentiability in genericdirections.",
    "The absoluteU reference, native sequentialexchange/globalreturn, fixedcircle and omittedcap are retained."
  ],
